00:14:15,950 --> 00:14:17,640
It turns out NVIDIA think so too.

148
00:14:17,806 --> 00:14:22,680
Next up, let's talk about something that came out of NVIDIA called stream render H3.

149
00:14:22,680 --> 00:14:26,580
This is actually a pretty similar concept to what we just looked at.

150
00:14:26,580 --> 00:14:32,620
It uses kind of that same split: Code runs the world, and then a video model draws it in real time.

151
00:14:32,910 --> 00:14:36,840
The difference with this one is how little the game actually hands the AI.

152
00:14:36,840 --> 00:14:40,040
Matrix game gives the model a blocky 3D render;

153
00:14:40,040 --> 00:14:43,280
NVIDIA gives it a color-coded map.

154
00:14:43,566 --> 00:14:45,440
